Cc: Monica Patel <monica@redwood.ai>, Marissa Cole <marissa@redwood.ai>
Date: Thu, 10 Dec 2026 16:12:00 -0800
Subject: SDK gateway transition — staging checklist + initial sample code

Sam — good to meet yesterday. Per our call, here’s a compact plan to move FastPay from the old SDK agent to the Redwood SDK gateway and cut over staging → production with minimal risk. I’ve attached a small staging config and a text file with sample snippets. High level:

- Goal: Route existing SDK calls to the Redwood API endpoint with a transparent shim (no code-level model changes for your app) and then flip DNS/canary once metrics look stable.
- Timeline: 2-week staging validation, 48-hour canary, full cutover on business hours.
- Success metrics: token latency p50 < 220ms, error-rate < 0.5% sustained, rate-limit errors < 0.1%.

Staging checklist (short):
1) SDK shim: point existing SDK config to redwood-staging.fastpay.internal (see attached sdkgateway-staging-config.yaml)
2) Instrumentation: enable token-level timing and capture X-RateLimit-* headers in logs
3) Retries: client 1 immediate retry + exponential backoff (base 200ms) with full jitter — more below
4) Timeouts: per-request 12s (hard) / per-stream 90s for streaming endpoints
5) Rate fencing: respect X-RateLimit-Remaining; backoff to 30s if header missing + increase sampling of server-side caching for repeated prefixes
6) Canary: 1% traffic → 10% → 50% → 100% with rollback guard on error-rate spikes

Quick sample (Node.js pseudo) — replace YOUR_KEY and endpoints per attached: 

const Redwood = require('@redwood/sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY, baseURL: 'https://staging-api.redwood.ai/v1' });

async function callModel(payload) {
  try {
    const res = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-small', input: payload, timeout: 12000 });
    return res;
  } catch (err) {
    // implement retry/backoff per policy (see below)
    throw err;
  }
}

I’ll be available to jump into a staging troubleshooting session next week. If you want, Monica can run the canary as CS lead and Marissa will be the implementation owner for code snippets and testing boilerplate.

—Karthik
